Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0029 (touches nvidia/dspark.py
only). VLLM_DSPARK_MAIN_PROJ_ROWPAR=1 (default off): the DSpark drafter's main_proj (the context combiner over the
three target taps, [5120, 15360], MXFP8 on Marlin) becomes a RowParallelLinear over the concatenated taps instead of a
ReplicatedLinear. Each rank multiplies its 7680 tap columns by the matching input rows (39 MB a rank instead of 79 MB:
the Oct 21 prose profile has main_proj at 366-385 us a round, ~210 GB/s) and one all-reduce of the [rows, 5120] partials
sums them (61 KB at 6 rows, on the RDMA ring), so ~-0.17 ms a round. No loader change: vLLM's RowParallelLinear loaders
cut the FP8 weight and its [32, 32] ue8m0 block scales on the input dim (7680 = 240 blocks a rank), as for 0028's
row-parallel Engram wkv. Engages at TP > 1 without sequence parallelism when the split keeps whole 32-column blocks;
otherwise a warning and the replicated layer. A drafter-only, rounding-class change (each rank's partial is rounded to
bf16 before the sum): the target's outputs are untouched, so greedy text is identical and only acceptance can move.

